IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 58, subsections (6) to (8.1) -- THE SURVIVOR'S PENSION AND A DISABILITY
-- PENSION PAYABLE TOGETHER.
--
-- Where a survivor's pension and a disability pension are both payable to the same person, the Act does not
-- add them: it fixes an aggregate and lets the second pension be whatever brings the two up to it. Subsection
-- (6) does so for a disability pension under this Act (the disability pension is the balance); subsection
-- (6.1) saves the person from being worse off than with the disability pension alone; subsection (6.2) is the
-- rule for earlier cases; subsection (7) lets the Minister pay the full disability pension instead and cut the
-- survivor's pension; subsections (8) and (8.1) are the mirror rules where the disability pension is paid under
-- a provincial pension plan (the survivor's pension is the balance).
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the flat rate benefits (s 56(2) and s 58(1.1), in this piece's other
-- modules, whose results the caller passes), the portions of the retirement pensions (ss 56, 58(3) to (3.6)),
-- the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (s 42(1),
-- s 18), the adjustment under s 45(2), the amounts payable under a provincial pension plan, the agreement under
-- s 80 (piece cp5), and the dates of death and of being deemed disabled (s 42(2), piece cp3).

§ `Section 58 (subsections 6 to 8.1) -- survivor's pension and disability pension payable together`

§§ `Parts of the aggregate`

-- Not a provision: the greater of two amounts plus 60% of the lesser, the shape of every term in the aggregates
-- of subsections (6) and (8): "(i) the greater of (A) and (B), and (ii) 60% of the lesser of (A) and (B)".
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp4 the greater of two amounts plus 60% of the lesser` first second MEANS
    (max first second) PLUS (60% TIMES (min first second))

§§ `Section 58(6) -- where a disability pension under this Act is also payable`

-- Subsection (6) applies where the contributor died, or the survivor is deemed to have become disabled, after 1997.
-- src:1851 | (6) Subject to subsection (6.1), where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a disability pension under this Act are payable to the survivor of a contributor and either the date of death of the contributor or the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act is after December 31, 1997, the amount of the disability pension is an amount that, when added to the amount of the survivor’s pension for a month in the year in which the survivor’s pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later, equals the aggregate of
@ref Act s 58(6) (src:1851)
GIVEN `the day of the death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58(6) — subsection (6) applies` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
        `the day of the death of the contributor` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1)
    OR  `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1)

