-- src:1850 | Calculation of disability pension where survivor’s pension payable
-- src:1851 | (6) Subject to subsection (6.1), where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a disability pension under this Act are payable to the survivor of a contributor and either the date of death of the contributor or the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act is after December 31, 1997, the amount of the disability pension is an amount that, when added to the amount of the survivor’s pension for a month in the year in which the survivor’s pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later, equals the aggregate of
@ref Act s 58(6) (src:1851)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(6) — the amount of the disability pension where a survivor's pension is also payable` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` MEANS
    -- "an amount that, when added to the amount of the survivor's pension ..., equals the aggregate of (a), (b) and (c)"
    ((`s 58(6)(a) — the aggregate for the flat rate benefits and the base portions` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted`)
        PLUS (`s 58(6)(b) — the aggregate for the first additional portions` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)`)
        PLUS (`s 58(6)(c) — the aggregate for the second additional portions` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)`))
    MINUS `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`

-- src:1873 | Saving
-- src:1874 | (6.1) Where subsection (6) applies and the aggregate amount of the survivor’s pension and the disability pension are less than the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor’s pension were not payable, the amount of the disability pension is the amount that results when
-- src:1875 | (a) the amount of the survivor’s pension
-- src:1876 | is subtracted from
-- src:1877 | (b) the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor’s pension were not payable.
@ref Act s 58(6.1) (src:1874-1877)
GIVEN `the amount of the disability pension under subsection (6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the survivor's pension` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(6.1) — the amount of the disability pension where the two pensions together are less than the disability pension alone` `the amount of the disability pension under subsection (6)` `the amount of the survivor's pension` `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable` MEANS
    IF (`the amount of the survivor's pension` PLUS `the amount of the disability pension under subsection (6)`) LESS THAN `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable`
    THEN `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable` MINUS `the amount of the survivor's pension`
    ELSE `the amount of the disability pension under subsection (6)`

-- src:1878 | Calculation of disability pension where survivor’s pension payable
-- src:1879 | (6.2) Where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a disability pension under this Act are payable to the survivor of a contributor and subsection (6) does not apply, the amount of the disability pension is an amount that, when added to the amount of the survivor’s pension for a month in the year in which the survivor’s pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later, equals the aggregate of
-- src:1880 | (a) the greater of
-- src:1881 | (i) the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i), and
-- src:1882 | (ii) the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a), and
-- src:1883 | (b) the lesser of
-- src:1884 | (i) the aggregate of the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii) and paragraph 56(1)(b), and
-- src:1885 | (ii) the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable, and for each of the two preceding years, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable.
@ref Act s 58(6.2) (src:1879-1885)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(6.2) — the amount of the disability pension where a survivor's pension is also payable and subsection (6) does not apply` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` MEANS
    ((max `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)`)
        PLUS (min `the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii) and paragraph 56(1)(b)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted`))
    MINUS `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`
    WHERE
        `the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii) and paragraph 56(1)(b)` MEANS
              (37.5% TIMES (  `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))
            PLUS (75% TIMES (  `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))

