`s 58(6), (6.1) and (6.2) — the amount of the disability pension payable with a survivor's pension` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable` MEANS
    -- Subsection (6.1) is a saving for a case in which (6) applies; (6.2) is the rule where (6) does not apply.
    IF `s 58(6) — subsection (6) applies` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act`
    THEN `s 58(6.1) — the amount of the disability pension where the two pensions together are less than the disability pension alone` (`s 58(6) — the amount of the disability pension where a survivor's pension is also payable` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`) `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` `the amount of the disability pension that would be payable if the survivor's pension were not payable`
    ELSE `s 58(6.2) — the amount of the disability pension where a survivor's pension is also payable and subsection (6) does not apply` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under paragraph 56(1)(a)` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the retirement pension portions of the disability pension under subsections 56(3), (3.1) and (3.2)` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` `the amount of the survivor's pension for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`

§§ `Section 58(7) -- special case`

-- src:1886 | Special case
-- src:1887 | (7) Notwithstanding subsection (6), the Minister may, in prescribed circumstances and on the written request of the applicant, if in the Minister’s opinion it would be to the applicant’s advantage, pay the applicant the full amount of the disability pension and calculate the amount of the applicant’s survivor’s pension in a manner similar to that set out in subsection (6) for the calculation of the disability pension, but in no case may the aggregate of the two pensions exceed what it would have been had subsection (6) applied.
@ref Act s 58(7) (src:1887)
GIVEN `the Minister may act in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has made a written request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Minister's opinion it would be to the applicant's advantage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of the survivor's pension and the disability pension under subsection (6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the full amount of the disability pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 58(7) — the survivor's pension where the Minister pays the full disability pension` `the Minister may act in prescribed circumstances` `the applicant has made a written request` `in the Minister's opinion it would be to the applicant's advantage` `the aggregate of the survivor's pension and the disability pension under subsection (6)` `the full amount of the disability pension` MEANS
    -- The survivor's pension is calculated "in a manner similar to that set out in subsection (6) for the
    -- calculation of the disability pension": the balance that brings the two up to the aggregate, which also
    -- keeps the aggregate from exceeding what it would have been under subsection (6). The prescribed
    -- circumstances are those of reg 54.4 (piece cr2); NOTHING where the Minister has no such power.
    IF   `the Minister may act in prescribed circumstances`
     AND `the applicant has made a written request`
     AND `in the Minister's opinion it would be to the applicant's advantage`
    THEN
        -- The aggregate is the survivor's pension plus the disability pension under subsection (6), as saved by (6.1).
        -- If the full disability pension is more than that aggregate, the text gives no survivor's pension (it
        -- would be negative, and the aggregate may not exceed the subsection (6) figure): NOTHING.
        IF `the full amount of the disability pension` GREATER THAN `the aggregate of the survivor's pension and the disability pension under subsection (6)`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the aggregate of the survivor's pension and the disability pension under subsection (6)` MINUS `the full amount of the disability pension`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 58(8) and (8.1) -- where a disability pension under a provincial pension plan is also payable`

-- src:1889 | (8) Except where otherwise provided by an agreement under section 80, where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a disability pension under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor of a contributor and either the date of death of the contributor or the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of a provincial pension plan is after December 31, 1997, the amount of the survivor’s pension is an amount that, when added to the amount of the disability pension for a month in the year in which the survivor’s pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later, equals the aggregate of
@ref Act s 58(8) (src:1889)
GIVEN `the day of the death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of a provincial pension plan` IS A DATE
      `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58(8) — subsection (8) applies` `the day of the death of the contributor` `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of a provincial pension plan` `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` MEANS
        (NOT `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise`)
    AND (   `the day of the death of the contributor` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1)
         OR `the date on which the survivor is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of a provincial pension plan` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1))

-- src:1890 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1891 | (i) the greater of
-- src:1892 | (A) the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i), and
-- src:1893 | (B) the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1894 | (ii) the lesser of
-- src:1895 | (A) the aggregate of
-- src:1896 | (I) the greater of
-- src:1897 | 1 the amount that would have been payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii), as the case may be, if the amounts referred to in clauses (1)(a)(ii)(B) and (C) or (a.1)(ii)(B) and (C), as the case may be, had not been included in the calculation made under that subparagraph, and
-- src:1898 | 2 the base portion of the contributor’s retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1899 | (II) 60% of the lesser of the amount described in subclause (I)(1) and the amount described in subclause (I)(2), and
-- src:1900 | (B) 75% of the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable,
-- src:1901 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:1902 | (i) the greater of
-- src:1903 | (A) the amount that would have been payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii), as the case may be, if the amounts referred to in clauses (1)(a)(ii)(A) and (C) or (a.1)(ii)(A) and (C), as the case may be, had not been included in the calculation made under that subparagraph, and
-- src:1904 | (B) the first additional portion of the contributor’s retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1905 | (ii) 60% of the lesser of the amount described in subclause (A) and the amount described in subclause (B), and
-- src:1906 | (c) the aggregate of
-- src:1907 | (i) the greater of
-- src:1908 | (A) the amount that would have been payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii), as the case may be, if the amounts referred to in clauses (1)(a)(ii)(A) and (B) or (a.1)(ii)(A) and (B), as the case may be, had not been included in the calculation made under that subparagraph, and
-- src:1909 | (B) the second additional portion of the contributor’s retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1910 | (ii) 60% of the lesser of the amount described in subclause (A) and the amount described in subclause (B).
@ref Act s 58(8) (src:1890-1910)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(8) — the amount of the survivor's pension where a disability pension is also payable under a provincial pension plan` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted` `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` MEANS
    -- The structure of subsection (6), with the provincial plan's flat rate benefit and portions for the disability side.
    ((max `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`)
        PLUS `the base term`
        PLUS `the first additional term`
        PLUS `the second additional term`)
    MINUS `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`
    WHERE
        `the base term` MEANS min (`cp4 the greater of two amounts plus 60% of the lesser` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`) (`the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`)) (75% TIMES `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the survivor's Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, adjusted`)
        `the first additional term` MEANS `cp4 the greater of two amounts plus 60% of the lesser` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`)
        `the second additional term` MEANS `cp4 the greater of two amounts plus 60% of the lesser` (37.5% TIMES `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`) (`the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`)

-- src:1911 | Calculation of survivor’s pension when disability pension payable under provincial pension plan
-- src:1912 | (8.1) Except where otherwise provided by an agreement under section 80, where a survivor’s pension under this Act and a disability pension under a provincial pension plan are payable to the survivor of a contributor and subsection (8) does not apply, the amount of the survivor’s pension is an amount that, when added to the amount of the disability pension for a month in the year in which the survivor’s pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later, equals the aggregate of
-- src:1913 | (a) the greater of
-- src:1914 | (i) the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i), and
-- src:1915 | (ii) the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1916 | (b) the lesser of
-- src:1917 | (i) the aggregate of
-- src:1918 | (A) the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii), and
-- src:1919 | (B) the portion of the contributor’s retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability, and
-- src:1920 | (ii) the amount of a benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable, and for each of the two preceding years, adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) as if the benefit had commenced to be payable in the later of the year in which the survivor first became qualified to receive the survivor’s pension and the year in which the survivor’s disability pension commenced to be payable.
@ref Act s 58(8.1) (src:1912-1920)
GIVEN `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` IS A `cp4 Retirement pension portions`
      `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 58(8.1) — the amount of the survivor's pension where a disability pension is also payable under a provincial pension plan and subsection (8) does not apply` `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)` `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted` `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later` MEANS
    ((max `the flat rate benefit payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (a.1)(i)` `the flat rate benefit payable under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`)
        PLUS (min `the aggregate of the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii) and the portion payable under the provincial pension plan` `the benefit of 25% of 1/12 of the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted`))
    MINUS `the amount of the disability pension under the provincial pension plan for a month in the year in which the survivor's pension or the disability pension commenced to be payable, whichever is the later`
    WHERE
        `the aggregate of the amounts payable under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) or (a.1)(ii) and the portion payable under the provincial pension plan` MEANS
              (37.5% TIMES (  `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                           PLUS `the contributor's retirement pension portions under subsections 58(3), (3.1) and (3.4)`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`))
            PLUS (  `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the base portion of a retirement pension`
                 PLUS `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the first additional portion of a retirement pension`
                 PLUS `the portions of the contributor's retirement pension payable to the survivor under the provincial pension plan in respect of disability`'s `cp4 the second additional portion of a retirement pension`)
